────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

--print now outputs just the answer with the default model: stdout is exactly P O N G (4 bytes), and the JSON response is "PONG". The evaluator was right that last round fixed nothing: I only tested with --model claude-opus-5-5 added, which answers cleanly. Run as written, with the default claude-opus-4-6, the bug was still there.

Cause: the extra newlines come from the model, not from yoyo. With --output-format stream-json, the provider's first text chunk is literally "\n\nPONG". That's why moving yoyo's own output to stderr last time couldn't remove them.

Fix (`src/main.rs`): a new helper, answer_payload, removes blank lines from the start of the answer. It's applied in the two places that write stdout in these modes: the --print output and the JSON response field. The first real line keeps its indentation, and everything after it is unchanged. I kept the trailing newline behaviour as it was, which means none is added.

Left alone on purpose: plain -p, piped input without --print, and the REPL stream the model's text straight to stdout, so they still show the leading newlines. --output files also keep the raw text.

Results after the fix, run from /tmp with no extra flags:
• `--print "Reply with exactly: PONG" → P O N G`
• `-p "Reply with exactly: PONG" → \n P O N G \n \n`
• piped, no --print → \n \n \n P O N G \n \n
• `-p ... --output-format json → "response":"PONG"`

Tests:
• A unit table for answer_payload covering indentation, blank lines in the middle, trailing newlines and empty input, plus a test that the JSON field gets the same treatment.
• A process-level test in tests/print_stdout_contract.rs that replays the model's "\n\n" + answer through a local stub. It checks the -p --print, piped --print and JSON paths by comparing raw stdout exactly (no trimming, no "contains"). It also asserts that the stub really sends the leading newlines, so it can't pass by accident.
• A test pinning that plain -p still passes the model's text through unchanged.
• A positive control, run in one command: when I made answer_payload return its input unchanged, the new process test and both unit tests failed by name, and they passed again once restored.

The fmt check, clippy with -D warnings, the build, the full cargo test and tests/harness_logic.sh all pass.

Docs: in ARCHITECTURE.md I kept the false "not reproduced" note visible, marked as wrong, and added the real measurements and the fix. An earlier note there that said the newlines' origin was unknown now points to this finding.

